# Copy to .env (Bun auto-loads ./.env from this directory on
# `bunx crewhaus run`). Fill in what you need.

# ── Model (required to RUN the agent) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Either works; ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN takes precedence if both are set.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=...

# ── Thredz wiki = the experts' long-term memory ───────────────────────────
# TWO keys, on purpose. Thredz allows ONE individual wiki space per API KEY,
# and thredz-mcp reads one THREDZ_API_KEY per PROCESS — so per-agent private
# memory means one key, and one server process, per agent:
#
#   THREDZ_API_KEY     → crewhaus.yaml, space `coffee-expert`
#   THREDZ_DAEMON_KEY  → daemon.yaml,   space `coffee-daemon`
#
# Each key needs a WIKI GRANT (read-write or admin): create the key, grant
# wiki access via /api/wiki/access, then create its space — over the API, or
# by letting the agent call `wiki_space_create` (justification-gated).
#
# Spaces need a Pro or Scale plan (Pro: 5 shared / 10 individual across up to
# 10 keys; Scale: 25 / 50 across up to 50 keys). Free and Starter have no
# spaces at all — drop `space:` from both specs and each key uses the
# account's unspaced wiki.
#
# Each spec resolves its own key at boot (fail-fast, exit 21 when unset) and
# delivers it to its synthesized `npx thredz-mcp` server.
THREDZ_API_KEY=
THREDZ_DAEMON_KEY=
# Self-hosted / local Thredz? Add base_url to the thredz: block in the spec:
#   thredz: { api_key: $THREDZ_API_KEY, space: coffee-expert, base_url: http://localhost:3000/api }

# ── Web research (required for /study and heartbeat STUDY to hit the web) ──
# The `researcher` sub-agent uses WebSearch/WebFetch. Provide a search
# provider + key (e.g. brave, tavily) per your CrewHaus setup.
CREWHAUS_SEARCH_PROVIDER=
CREWHAUS_SEARCH_API_KEY=

# ── Slack (only for the daemon.yaml channel daemon) ───────────────────────
SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=
SLACK_SIGNING_SECRET=
